invariant: INV-41
file: src/rsa_mont.c
catches: rsa_avx2_model_test
reason: base_times_power_of_two_mod leaves out the subtraction that brings a
  base at or above m below m. times_word_mod's estimate then can pass the
  quotient by more than 2, and the two passes that add m back leave a
  remainder that is not the base times 2^64 mod m. Only a signature at or
  above m shows it, and the verifiers refuse one before rsa_vp1_cpu, so
  bin/rsa_avx2_model_test hands rsa_vp1_cpu the signatures m and
  2^(64k) - 1 under CH_CPU_AVX2 and requires rsa_vp1's bytes.

--- old
    rsa_mont64_reduce_once(power, power, mod);
    for (size_t i = 0; i < steps; i++) {
--- new
    for (size_t i = 0; i < steps; i++) {
